+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional alias expression is supplied with the
+   ``canonical`` option and is parsed as a Python type expression. A type alias
+   can be documented inside a class; its body describes the alias but does not
+   establish a further nested namespace. For example::
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+      .. py:class:: User
+
+         .. py:type:: Name
+            :canonical: str
+
+   The ``canonical`` option also registers its value as an aliased target for
+   Python cross-references.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: Python type expression
+
+      The optional expression represented by the alias. Names in the expression
+      are parsed as Python type references.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:exception:: name
                    .. py:exception:: name(parameters)
                    .. py:exception:: name[type parameters](parameters)
